/**
 * Both engines, asked about real code rather than about code written to ask them.
 *
 * A corpus written to exercise a graph model exercises what its author thought of,
 * and a codebase does not have that limit: peq's own sources hold the constructs it
 * happens to use, in the proportions real code uses them, which is the part of the
 * question a curated corpus cannot answer. The analyses are run by the data provider
 * so that the reference engine's own cost is not measured as test time.
 *
 * @internal
 */
